\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  What grace, O Lord, and beauty shone
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Around Thy steps below!
\par What patient love was seen in all
\par Thy life and death of woe!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. For ever on Thy burdened heart
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 A weight of sorrow hung,
\par Yet no ungentle, murmuring word
\par Escaped Thy silent tongue.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thy foes might hate, despise, revile,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Thy friends unfaithful prove:
\par   Unwearied in forgiveness still,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Thy heart could only love.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O give us hearts to love like Thee,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Like Thee, O Lord, to grieve
\par Far more for others sins than all
\par The wrongs that we receive.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. One with Thyself, may every eye
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 In us, Thy brethren, see
\par That gentleness and grace that spring
\par From union, Lord, with Thee.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

